{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Even given all these tests, some studies have raised doubts about the diagnostic accuracy of these conventional approaches, especially in the critically ill patient population [13, 14].",
      "reason": "The Introduction describes current knowledge (conventional diagnostic workup, its limitations, high mortality) and the uncertainty regarding diagnostic accuracy, motivating the review."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Therefore, we conducted a high-quality, comprehensive systematic review and meta-analysis that included the most recent publications that reported clinical outcomes with the use of PoCUS in patients who developed acute onset dyspnea.",
      "reason": "The need for the review is explicitly explained: rapid diagnosis is of utmost importance, conventional approaches have doubtful accuracy, and few trials have examined clinical outcomes (text_3: 'very few trials have examined meaningful clinical outcomes related to PoCUS usage to date')."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "In addition to the existing diagnostic accuracy studies [16-20, 25], our main objective, as a new insight to this field, was to investigate how PoCUS improves clinical endpoints in patients with acute onset dyspnea.",
      "reason": "Existing reviews/diagnostic accuracy studies are cited and the distinct need for the current review (clinical outcomes vs diagnostic accuracy) is explained; text_19 further contrasts with previous reviews [16-20, 60]."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "PoCUS has other advantages, such as being free from ionizing radiation, and most importantly can be performed in real-time at the bedside [16, 21]. Additionally, PoCUS can answer a broad spectrum of remaining diagnostic questions and may also help to optimize and personalize therapy [22].",
      "reason": "The mechanism by which PoCUS may improve outcomes (real-time bedside imaging enabling faster diagnosis and therapy optimization) is briefly described in the introduction."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a review of a diagnostic intervention (PoCUS) rather than a complex multi-component intervention or delivery context; no logic model requirement applies and none is reported."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 88
}

